# Viewport Synchronization Test Plan

## The Theory
The disjointed thumbnail loading during scrolling/"pulling through" occurs because the Semantic View and Grid View calculate their in-view items differently. Specifically, the Semantic View's `itemAt()` hit-testing logic in QML may be reporting an incorrect visual range (missing rows or calculating indices wrong). When the C++ backend receives this incorrect range, the `VisibleRangeManager` aggressively cancels or deprioritizes image decodes for thumbnails that are *actually* on-screen, causing visual pop-in or stuttering.

## Test Design: "Prove the Disconnect"

To definitively prove if the QML Viewport is lying to the C++ Backend about what's on screen, we will implement the following 3-stage test:

### 1. QML-Side Visual Tracers
In [test_scrollbench/qml/GalleryViewSemanticScrollBench.qml](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/qml/GalleryViewSemanticScrollBench.qml) and [GalleryViewScrollBench.qml](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/qml/GalleryViewScrollBench.qml):
- We will modify [updateVisibleRange()](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.cpp#620-669) to log precise hits.
- We will add a temporary debug visualizer (e.g., highlighting the first and last detected rows in green/red) so you can visually see *exactly* what QML thinks the boundaries are when you scroll fast.

### 2. C++ Range Manager Interception
In [test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.cpp](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.cpp) ([updateVisibleRange](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/test_scrollbench/src/ScrollBenchImageModel.cpp#620-669)):
- We will inject logging that prints the delta between the requested viewport range and the currently loaded tiles.
- We will track if the Semantic View's proxy indices are misaligned with the source model's flat indices.

### 3. Execution & Verification
In [src/AsyncImageProvider.cpp](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/src/AsyncImageProvider.cpp):
- We will log a high-priority warning (`qWarning`) every time an `AsyncImageProvider::requestImage` call is blocked/deprioritized because `VisibleRangeManager::isPathVisible()` returned `false`.
- **The Smoking Gun**: If you see images blank on your screen, but the console shows `[AsyncImageProvider] Rejecting decode for <image> - VRM says it is out of view`, we will have 100% proven the theory that the viewport hit-testing is structurally misaligned.

